### F-WRK-002 [P1] [Reliability] Retry and terminal failure behavior is modeled but not operationalized consistently

**Remediation status:** Fixed

**Remediation summary:**
Background workers now share an operational retry and dead-letter path. Added retry metadata fields, migration `0093`, a `dead_lettered` job status, deterministic exponential backoff with bounded jitter, worker-facing failure handling that either schedules the next retry or dead-letters after max attempts, queryable status filtering, manual replay for failed/dead-lettered jobs, and cancellation for failed/dead-lettered jobs. Workflow jobs now default to three attempts, failed workflow runs are reset to queued when their backing job is scheduled for retry, and exhausted workflow jobs remain failed while their backing job enters the queryable DLQ state.

